+    hold; a branch back to a loop head also loads any the head holds and the
+    branch does not (after a call inside the loop). So a loop keeps its
+    registers in host registers from one pass to the next. A merged chunk's
+    start that no goto names is entered only by falling into it (its other
+    entries are its own function) and joins nothing.
